Z||000000||Tabs31||11-25-2001||06:32 PM||||Has anybody put coil over springs on their fiero??? and are they really easy to raise and lower???<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tabs31_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||banditbalz||11-25-2001||07:07 PM||||Jonathon McCreery (slammedfiero) is using Ground Control coil overs. His ride is one of the lowest I've ever seen. Handles awesome! No ride quality to speak of. All of these characteristics can be dialed one way or the other with a lift of the rear end.<BR>I plan on going Ground Control this spring. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  You interested in my Eibach springs?<P><BR><P>------------------<BR>Silver 86 GT<BR>completely stock,<BR>completely fast!||||reg||1
Z||000002||fierochild||11-25-2001||09:09 PM||||Hey Tabs,<BR>     I put Held Motor Sport 300lb coilovers on KYB struts on my 86 GT.  Love the improved handleing. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">  Ride is very firm, but enjoyable.  I would say it rides about like a Vette.  I normally rou with the springs lowered 2".  When autocrossing I jack up the car, unlock the ring, and dial in the setting that works best for the track.  You can buy a special spanner wrench which makes it possible to make the adjustment with out raising the car.  In addition to the rear coilovers, I did polly on the cradle and rear suspension, added a Fiero front swaybar to the rear, removed the steering dampner, and moved the battery up front. The car handles like a dream. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  This winter I plan to ploy the front suspension and install new ball joints.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/fierochildsig_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||the need for speed||11-26-2001||11:32 AM|||| hi I just bought koni shocks and Eibach springs.I want to go with wider tires in the rear.so my question is do I have to buy a new setup shocks/springs or can I keep the koni and by just coil overs that will work with them? and were do I look for coil overs?Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000004||FieroBUZZ||11-26-2001||02:16 PM||||George, please let me know if you want to get rid of your Eibachs.  I'll take them.<P>Fierochild: nice two tone paint in you sig. I'd like to do that but haven't decided where the break will be. Either hood/roof or down to the moldings.<P>Gary||||reg||14
